{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01474m8BX7iknRpShvbnkHys","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: casegraphen-orchestrate\n3\tdescription: Route multi-phase or ambiguous CaseGraphen work across the direct task skills while preserving exact revisions, artifacts, unresolved evidence, and review seams. Use for end-to-end workflows that may span design, audit, external-runtime integration, governed memory, and operation. It coordinates handoffs only; it never accepts, reviews, rebases, broadens authority, or reimplements CaseGraphen's deterministic rules.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# Orchestrate a governed CaseGraphen process\n7\t\n8\tUse this process skill only when the request spans multiple phases or the next\n9\tdirect task skill is not yet known. If the user asks for one bounded task, invoke\n10\tthat task skill directly. Read [routing.md](references/routing.md) before choosing\n11\ta route and [handoff.md](references/handoff.md) before crossing a phase boundary.\n12\t\n13\t## Contract\n14\t\n15\t- Route and carry context; do not reproduce graph lint, completeness, retry,\n16\t  review, gate, temporal, authority, or acceptance rules.\n17\t- Never review or accept a proposal, silently rebase a stale revision, enable a\n18\t  worker, widen scope, or grant authority. These are explicit return seams.\n19\t- Automatic continuation is allowed only between read-only or proposal-only\n20\t  phases when the handoff is complete and no review or authority seam is open.\n21\t- Every boundary emits `skill.orchestration_handoff.v0`, validated against\n22\t  [skill.orchestration_handoff.v0.schema.json](references/skill.orchestration_handoff.v0.schema.json).\n23\t- The handoff records facts observed from tools separately from unresolved\n24\t  evidence and runtime-declared claims. It never turns either into accepted state.\n25\t\n26\t## Workflow\n27\t\n28\t1. Classify the request as a direct task or a multi-phase process. For a direct\n29\t   task, name the selected task skill and stop orchestrating.\n30\t2. Pin the exact case-space id and observed revision when available. Inventory\n31\t   topology, reports, artifacts, content hashes, and unresolved evidence without\n32\t   inventing missing values.\n33\t3. Select exactly one next task skill using the routing table. State why it owns\n34\t   the phase and which responsibilities remain outside it.\n35\t4. Run or hand off to that skill. Preserve its outputs as artifacts; do not\n36\t   reinterpret a proposal, report, or runtime declaration as accepted evidence.\n37\t5. Emit a strict handoff using the example in\n38\t   [skill.orchestration_handoff.v0.example.json](references/skill.orchestration_handoff.v0.example.json).\n39\t6. If `return_required` is true, return to the named human/policy/authority seam.\n40\t   Otherwise continue only when `next_action.kind` is `invoke_task_skill`.\n41\t7. Finish only after the selected task skill reports its own completion and the\n42\t   handoff contains no unresolved required evidence or open seam.\n43\t\n44\t## Representative routes\n45\t\n46\t```text\n47\tnative:\n48\t  intake -> casegraphen-design -> topology_review -> casegraphen-operate\n49\t\n50\texternal runtime:\n51\t  intake -> casegraphen-design -> topology_review -> external runtime\n52\t         -> casegraphen-integrate -> casegraphen-audit -> evidence_review\n53\t         -> casegraphen-operate\n54\t```\n55\t\n56\tMemory query, curation, and audit use the same routing and seam rules. Memory\n57\tproposals still require the existing independent review and gated operation path.\n58\t\n59\t## Stop and return\n60\t\n61\tReturn rather than continue when any of these is true:\n62\t\n63\t- topology, evidence, plan, or memory review is required;\n64\t- the observed revision is stale or missing for a mutation;\n65\t- worker enablement, capability, credential, scope, or authority must change;\n66\t- a hard conflict or required evidence remains unresolved;\n67\t- a task skill refuses, or the requested next action is outside its boundary.\n68\t\n69\tThe process skill coordinates the lifecycle. `casegraphen-operate` remains the\n70\tsingle task skill that owns the shared revision, operation-gate, mutation, and\n71\trefusal protocol; it is intentionally not split.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a61ca99-e520-41d9-8101-5f6aac26c72c","uuid":"0f9148be-8f68-4989-adcd-f4a1e01db301","timestamp":"2026-08-06T08:40:37.731Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/2c/qtwpt9yj4fs9k20l__sg_zd40000gn/T/casegraphen-eval-native-case-lifecycle-89_zvxe_/workspace/skill/casegraphen-orchestrate/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: casegraphen-orchestrate\ndescription: Route multi-phase or ambiguous CaseGraphen work across the direct task skills while preserving exact revisions, artifacts, unresolved evidence, and review seams. Use for end-to-end workflows that may span design, audit, external-runtime integration, governed memory, and operation. It coordinates handoffs only; it never accepts, reviews, rebases, broadens authority, or reimplements CaseGraphen's deterministic rules.\n---\n\n# Orchestrate a governed CaseGraphen process\n\nUse this process skill only when the request spans multiple phases or the next\ndirect task skill is not yet known. If the user asks for one bounded task, invoke\nthat task skill directly. Read [routing.md](references/routing.md) before choosing\na route and [handoff.md](references/handoff.md) before crossing a phase boundary.\n\n## Contract\n\n- Route and carry context; do not reproduce graph lint, completeness, retry,\n  review, gate, temporal, authority, or acceptance rules.\n- Never review or accept a proposal, silently rebase a stale revision, enable a\n  worker, widen scope, or grant authority. These are explicit return seams.\n- Automatic continuation is allowed only between read-only or proposal-only\n  phases when the handoff is complete and no review or authority seam is open.\n- Every boundary emits `skill.orchestration_handoff.v0`, validated against\n  [skill.orchestration_handoff.v0.schema.json](references/skill.orchestration_handoff.v0.schema.json).\n- The handoff records facts observed from tools separately from unresolved\n  evidence and runtime-declared claims. It never turns either into accepted state.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Classify the request as a direct task or a multi-phase process. For a direct\n   task, name the selected task skill and stop orchestrating.\n2. Pin the exact case-space id and observed revision when available. Inventory\n   topology, reports, artifacts, content hashes, and unresolved evidence without\n   inventing missing values.\n3. Select exactly one next task skill using the routing table. State why it owns\n   the phase and which responsibilities remain outside it.\n4. Run or hand off to that skill. Preserve its outputs as artifacts; do not\n   reinterpret a proposal, report, or runtime declaration as accepted evidence.\n5. Emit a strict handoff using the example in\n   [skill.orchestration_handoff.v0.example.json](references/skill.orchestration_handoff.v0.example.json).\n6. If `return_required` is true, return to the named human/policy/authority seam.\n   Otherwise continue only when `next_action.kind` is `invoke_task_skill`.\n7. Finish only after the selected task skill reports its own completion and the\n   handoff contains no unresolved required evidence or open seam.\n\n## Representative routes\n\n```text\nnative:\n  intake -> casegraphen-design -> topology_review -> casegraphen-operate\n\nexternal runtime:\n  intake -> casegraphen-design -> topology_review -> external runtime\n         -> casegraphen-integrate -> casegraphen-audit -> evidence_review\n         -> casegraphen-operate\n```\n\nMemory query, curation, and audit use the same routing and seam rules. Memory\nproposals still require the existing independent review and gated operation path.\n\n## Stop and return\n\nReturn rather than continue when any of these is true:\n\n- topology, evidence, plan, or memory review is required;\n- the observed revision is stale or missing for a mutation;\n- worker enablement, capability, credential, scope, or authority must change;\n- a hard conflict or required evidence remains unresolved;\n- a task skill refuses, or the requested next action is outside its boundary.\n\nThe process skill coordinates the lifecycle. `casegraphen-operate` remains the\nsingle task skill that owns the shared revision, operation-gate, mutation, and\nrefusal protocol; it is intentionally not split.\n","numLines":72,"startLine":1,"totalLines":72}}}
